WEBVTT

00:15.630 --> 00:18.460
I never dreamed before

00:18.460 --> 00:21.300
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.300 --> 00:24.870
into the world of perfect free

00:24.870 --> 00:26.970
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:26.970 --> 00:29.810
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.810 --> 00:32.540
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.540 --> 00:36.110
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.110 --> 00:37.280
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.280 --> 00:40.190
I was made to hit in America

00:40.190 --> 00:43.050
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.050 --> 00:48.960
I was made to hit in America

00:48.960 --> 00:52.630
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.630 --> 00:54.630
(To me, forever)

00:54.630 --> 00:58.340
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.340 --> 01:01.570
(To me, forever)

01:08.410 --> 01:14.020
I was made to hit in America

01:14.020 --> 01:16.860
I was made to hit in America

01:16.860 --> 01:19.720
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.720 --> 01:22.530
I was made to hit in America

01:22.530 --> 01:25.300
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.300 --> 01:33.170
I was made to hit in America

01:42.210 --> 01:46.210
Belle Ame...It means
"beautiful spirit" in French.

01:47.720 --> 01:49.740
Bugger off. Hit the road.

01:51.390 --> 01:53.730
-Jim, give me that!
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

01:53.730 --> 01:55.160
-Hey! They're waiting for us.
-After all, Eddy is just a guy.

01:55.160 --> 01:58.160
-Why are you saying this now? Shit!
-But, that makes Dying Breed appealing.

01:58.160 --> 02:02.830
-What shall we do? That's irresponsible.
Hey Jim! What are you filming!?
-On top of that, Matt is wild.

02:04.740 --> 02:09.410
Like a river flowing,
inspiration always flows from my mind.

02:09.410 --> 02:13.410
-Hey! Dancing, dancing...Party man...
-Oh! He's a funny guy.

02:13.410 --> 02:17.710
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...
-Happy birthday to you...

02:21.590 --> 02:26.260
Sometimes, there comes a special day,
while they're on tour.

02:26.260 --> 02:29.090
It's a beautiful scene.

02:29.090 --> 02:33.270
Tokyo...a city of noise
and chaos. Techno-city.

02:33.270 --> 02:34.170
Come on!

02:34.170 --> 02:36.700
They had a live here, as well.

02:36.700 --> 02:39.190
In the evening, with the shining moon.

02:40.610 --> 02:44.510
They met a boy. It was
a very special event.

03:06.560 --> 03:09.530
"Fishing Hole"

03:24.250 --> 03:30.260
A long time ago, a female office worker
quit her job for no good reason...

03:30.260 --> 03:32.360
and started the
Grateful Sound Summer Special

03:32.360 --> 03:34.260
with some music-lover friends.

03:35.590 --> 03:39.360
It all started when she was blown away
by the Glastonbury Festival in England,

03:39.360 --> 03:43.540
and wondered if fans couldn't put together
a pure rock festival here in Japan.

03:43.540 --> 03:47.440
Grateful Sound started
from that simple motive.

03:49.840 --> 03:54.210
Nowadays, it's the biggest
outdoor event in Japan.

03:54.210 --> 03:56.780
Are you that office worker?

03:56.780 --> 04:02.220
No...She was my sister,
who died last year.

04:02.220 --> 04:03.380
I see...

04:05.560 --> 04:08.860
Sorry for being so blunt,
but I have to talk business.

04:08.860 --> 04:10.060
Sure...

04:10.060 --> 04:13.430
You're friends with a member
of Dying Breed, aren't you?

04:13.430 --> 04:14.570
Huh?

04:14.570 --> 04:18.070
I heard that two of their members
were at your live performance.

04:18.070 --> 04:19.400
Yeah...

04:19.400 --> 04:24.740
Couldn't you get them, Dying Breed,
to come to the Grateful Sound event?

04:24.740 --> 04:26.580
What?!

04:26.580 --> 04:28.880
They just finished their
world tour and are off now.

04:28.880 --> 04:29.580
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'”

04:28.880 --> 04:29.580
They just finished their
world tour and are off now.

04:29.580 --> 04:33.420
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'”

04:29.580 --> 04:33.420
Yeah...I know that, but I'm asking...

04:33.420 --> 04:33.940
"Live 20
'Grateful Sound'"

04:33.420 --> 04:33.940
Hm...

04:33.940 --> 04:34.500
Hm...

04:36.910 --> 04:40.920
Nowadays, Grateful Sound seems
like just a money-making tool.

04:40.920 --> 04:44.220
I feel like it's moving
in the wrong direction.

04:46.090 --> 04:48.590
Ran, the Japanese producer,

04:48.590 --> 04:52.930
is planning to push one of the bands on
his label-a boring band called Belle Ame

04:52.930 --> 04:57.920
featuring a young actor
named Yoshito Morozumi.

05:00.270 --> 05:03.270
You know, my sister was someone...

05:03.270 --> 05:07.640
who thought that music could change
the world consciousness of people.

05:08.780 --> 05:15.120
Ran and Leon Sykes' RJ label can
only produce "feel-good" pop tunes.

05:15.120 --> 05:18.020
"Escapist" music that
says everything is all right

05:18.020 --> 05:19.990
just paralyzes people's consciousness

05:19.990 --> 05:22.290
and steals away their ability
to solve the problems

05:22.290 --> 05:24.060
that they face in their everyday lives.

05:24.060 --> 05:25.120
Yeah...

05:27.400 --> 05:31.230
Of course, it doesn't really matter

05:31.230 --> 05:34.800
that there are so many "feel-good"
pop groups out there...

05:34.800 --> 05:40.410
...but I don't want Grateful Sound
taken over by groups like those.

05:40.410 --> 05:43.910
You say music has the power
to change the world?

05:43.910 --> 05:49.710
Yes...At least Dying Breed does!

05:52.750 --> 05:55.020
I like you, Aunty...

05:56.320 --> 05:58.260
A-Aunty?!

05:58.260 --> 06:00.760
I'll get in touch with Eddy right away.

06:00.760 --> 06:02.260
You will?!

06:02.260 --> 06:05.600
That is, if you let us
perform at Grateful Sound.

06:08.770 --> 06:09.760
-Oh!
-Oh!

06:13.610 --> 06:17.950
Actually...After hearing
Mongolian Chop Squad's CD,

06:17.950 --> 06:23.290
I brought up your name, at one time...

06:23.290 --> 06:27.690
To replace Loud Crime City,
who suddenly broke up.

06:29.460 --> 06:34.960
Of course, your quality doesn't even
touch that of the other pro bands...

06:34.960 --> 06:37.570
Hmm...Hmph!

06:37.570 --> 06:40.740
Considering your future
possibilities and low cost,

06:40.740 --> 06:43.570
there were some who agreed with me.

06:43.570 --> 06:45.410
Mm...

06:45.410 --> 06:47.080
-But...
-Huh?

06:47.080 --> 06:48.670
Ran overruled me.

06:51.750 --> 06:53.920
I don't know the reason,
but in this industry,

06:53.920 --> 06:56.080
if you get on the wrong side of Ran,

06:56.080 --> 06:58.420
it could be difficult getting ahead.

06:59.420 --> 07:01.510
That's why I want to do it.

07:03.930 --> 07:09.520
With backup from you and Leon,
it won't be impossible.

07:10.930 --> 07:15.270
I think he said he'd stop by in two weeks,
on his way back from Australia...

07:17.610 --> 07:20.780
I've decided! I'm going to
negotiate with Leon Sykes.

07:20.780 --> 07:23.280
I hope you'll help us too, Aunty...

07:23.280 --> 07:27.150
Aunty? My name is Kazuo Sato!

07:30.950 --> 07:32.120
Wasn't it great?

07:32.120 --> 07:34.290
Yeah. Eddy's so awesome!

07:34.290 --> 07:36.120
What about Matt?

07:36.120 --> 07:37.390
A little scary, I think.

07:37.390 --> 07:39.890
And that boy who sang...Who is he?

07:39.890 --> 07:42.230
I've never heard of Yukiko...

07:42.230 --> 07:43.400
You too, Atsuko?

07:43.400 --> 07:45.900
What? You're performing
at Grateful Sound?

07:45.900 --> 07:49.740
Yeah, well...I'm getting together
with a new band called Belle Ame.

07:49.740 --> 07:52.240
We plan to release an album this Fall.

07:52.240 --> 07:54.640
-A singer?
-That's great!

07:56.180 --> 07:59.410
-Umm...
-Let's see...
Let's get something to eat.

07:59.410 --> 08:01.850
Oh...I pass.

08:01.850 --> 08:04.650
Huh? What a wet blanket...

08:04.650 --> 08:06.640
I'm kinda worried
about Ryusuke-kun's injuries.

08:08.420 --> 08:11.930
Ah...I was just watching a movie...

08:11.930 --> 08:13.090
So long!

08:13.090 --> 08:15.100
What, from now?

08:15.100 --> 08:19.530
Maho...Eguchi-san,
Yohei Takami and Chiemi Kuniyoshi

08:19.530 --> 08:20.770
are at that place I told you about.

08:20.770 --> 08:28.610
Oh? They have a terrific salad there. Oh...
I think Koyuki likes Chiemi Kuniyoshi...

08:28.610 --> 08:30.950
I have all her CDs. I'm her biggest fan!

08:30.950 --> 08:33.950
Oh, didn't you say you were
worried about Ryusuke's injuries?

08:33.950 --> 08:36.120
He just needs to put some spit on them!

08:36.120 --> 08:40.710
Um...Sorry, but no outsiders...

08:43.220 --> 08:45.920
Oh...Then...

08:49.230 --> 08:51.060
Tell Ryusuke I said "Hi."

09:25.100 --> 09:27.100
Well, it'll all work out.

09:27.100 --> 09:29.600
Listen, how can you be so sure?

09:29.600 --> 09:30.500
I dunno.

09:32.110 --> 09:35.110
Can't you give us a good explanation?!

09:35.110 --> 09:38.370
When you're hungry,
you get snippy, don't you?!

09:41.550 --> 09:44.720
You wanted to meet
Chiemi Kuniyoshi so much?

09:44.720 --> 09:47.690
Yeah...I don't think
I'll be able to sleep tonight.

09:54.560 --> 09:56.560
I...

09:56.560 --> 09:58.230
I had a dream once...

10:03.740 --> 10:09.080
There was a wide open space
that seemed to be veiled by mist,

10:09.080 --> 10:10.840
and there was lots of trash...

10:13.580 --> 10:17.750
Hot!! Damn you!
Are you trying to kill me?!

10:17.750 --> 10:20.920
That trash...They were
picking it up, right?

10:20.920 --> 10:24.090
The spirits of dead rockers...

10:24.090 --> 10:26.090
-Huh?
-Huh?

10:26.090 --> 10:29.930
"We're cleaning up after
your concert," they said.

10:31.770 --> 10:34.290
Sid was doing it like he
didn't really want to, right?

10:36.370 --> 10:41.210
A-After I saw that dream,
my fever had gone down and...

10:44.880 --> 10:47.880
I don't know how they feel about it,

10:47.880 --> 10:51.840
but there are bands that are
born from miraculous encounters.

10:53.220 --> 10:55.210
Not anyone would do.

10:56.220 --> 10:58.090
They're the only ones who could do it.

11:08.770 --> 11:14.410
Hey, wait a minute!
I never saw a dream like that!

11:14.410 --> 11:20.580
I-I always dream in panoramic,
full-color, 3-D.

11:20.580 --> 11:26.750
I haven't seen any dream that foretells
our performance at Grateful Sound!

11:26.750 --> 11:31.530
Uh, Chiba-kun, it's just a dream...

11:31.530 --> 11:35.100
But! I'm the only one
who didn't have that dream...

11:35.100 --> 11:36.930
Chiba-kun, your noodles are getting mushy.

11:36.930 --> 11:38.700
Shut up, will you!

11:38.700 --> 11:41.270
So was that dream
in black and white? Color?

11:41.270 --> 11:43.640
Hm...I wonder...

11:44.940 --> 11:45.940
Probably color.

11:45.940 --> 11:48.200
What the heck...Aw, forget it!

12:19.640 --> 12:20.630
Huh?

12:23.980 --> 12:28.180
What is it? Someone fooling around?

12:39.260 --> 12:41.160
Ouch!

12:42.760 --> 12:43.660
Yo!

12:45.770 --> 12:48.600
Oh...I'm so sorry!

12:50.610 --> 12:52.640
You've gotta be quiet,
or you'll wake my mother.

12:52.640 --> 12:53.630
Yeah...

12:55.440 --> 12:57.450
You're okay now, Ryusuke-kun?

12:57.450 --> 12:59.110
Yeah, well...

12:59.110 --> 13:02.780
Why'd you two drop in like this?

13:02.780 --> 13:08.120
Well...I wanted to see
your surprised face!

13:08.120 --> 13:08.960
Here!

13:08.960 --> 13:11.360
Huh? What is it?

13:11.360 --> 13:12.790
"Kuniyoshi"

13:12.790 --> 13:13.360
"Kuniyoshi"

13:12.790 --> 13:13.360
It's the real thing.

13:13.360 --> 13:14.350
It's the real thing.

13:16.300 --> 13:20.630
This...Could this be?

13:21.800 --> 13:23.940
It's Chiemi Kuniyoshi's autograph.

13:23.940 --> 13:25.100
Wow!

13:26.640 --> 13:28.480
Hey...Your folks are gonna get up.

13:28.480 --> 13:29.670
W-What's she like?

13:31.250 --> 13:36.420
Mm...Well...A nice girl,
like she is on television.

13:36.420 --> 13:37.590
Ah...

13:37.590 --> 13:39.610
She said to tell you "Hi."

13:41.760 --> 13:45.430
I'm going to treasure it.
Thanks a lot, Maho.

13:45.430 --> 13:46.420
Hm?

13:53.940 --> 13:57.230
"The moment the scent...
of excitement explodes..."

13:53.940 --> 13:57.230
Boy, you've really grown up, haven't you?

13:58.940 --> 14:00.610
Stupid brother...

14:00.610 --> 14:05.110
Koyuki...Why was this magazine
by your pillow?

14:05.110 --> 14:06.240
No reason...

14:07.450 --> 14:09.420
Oh...I'm beat.

14:11.450 --> 14:15.460
Koyuki, can I stay overnight?

14:15.460 --> 14:18.630
Huh? But I've got only one bed.

14:18.630 --> 14:23.300
Well, y'see...Ryusuke's bedding stinks
and it's full of lice.

14:23.300 --> 14:24.200
Shut up.

14:25.730 --> 14:27.220
Besides, Ryusuke's here too.

14:28.640 --> 14:34.170
No. I'm going home. I can't
sleep in a strange bed.

14:38.650 --> 14:41.050
Okay, well...Take care of her.

14:42.750 --> 14:44.310
Ray!

14:45.590 --> 14:49.420
Ouch...Listen, I'm injured, you know...

14:49.420 --> 14:50.860
Take care...

14:52.430 --> 14:53.550
See ya later.

14:55.260 --> 14:56.890
Be careful...

15:09.280 --> 15:11.110
Say, do you have something
I can change into?

15:11.110 --> 15:12.880
Uh, just a minute...

15:24.630 --> 15:27.960
I...I'm going to do some composing...

15:28.630 --> 15:30.960
Okay. Well, good night.

16:21.620 --> 16:26.280
Koyuki? Come over here,
if you're going to sleep.

16:27.490 --> 16:28.650
Huh?

16:35.960 --> 16:36.950
'Kay...

16:54.580 --> 16:56.920
Koyuki...

16:56.920 --> 16:59.420
-Koyuki...
-Huh?

16:59.420 --> 17:03.620
You really looked great
in that movie, Koyuki.

17:07.430 --> 17:11.300
Truly...You looked really great.

17:12.600 --> 17:14.120
Thanks...

17:24.780 --> 17:26.280
You know...

17:26.280 --> 17:33.290
We kissed that day...
What did that mean?

17:33.290 --> 17:37.820
Or, what do I mean to you?
Maho...Are you asleep?

18:25.040 --> 18:28.530
"Thank you, Koyuki.
6:30 a.m. I'm going home. Maho"

18:38.220 --> 18:42.210
You really looked great
in that movie, Koyuki.

18:44.890 --> 18:47.560
Mm...Good morning...

18:47.560 --> 18:48.830
Good morning.

18:48.830 --> 18:49.960
Good morning.

18:52.230 --> 18:54.060
-What?!
-Quit dawdling, will you?

18:55.570 --> 18:57.910
Hurry up and wash your face and eat.

18:57.910 --> 18:59.570
Y-Yeah...

18:59.570 --> 19:02.740
Maho-chan...
Please help yourself to seconds.

19:02.740 --> 19:03.910
Thank you.

19:03.910 --> 19:09.080
My mother, that night, was really scary.

19:09.080 --> 19:12.590
Listen to me! When a man is going
to act like a full-fledged man...

19:12.590 --> 19:15.760
-he has to be able
to take full responsibility...
-Yes, ma'am...

19:15.760 --> 19:16.950
Yes...

19:28.600 --> 19:31.900
Hey, I don't see baldy
with golden teeth today.

19:40.210 --> 19:42.880
You showed up in front of me again...

19:42.880 --> 19:44.370
You must be crazy.

19:46.550 --> 19:49.060
I brought the Beck's favorite today.

19:49.060 --> 19:50.220
Hmph...

19:50.220 --> 19:53.230
Beck is super shy
and gets so lonely easily.

19:53.230 --> 19:55.230
Maybe because it came
from the way he looks.

19:55.230 --> 19:56.790
So take good care of him.

19:59.570 --> 20:04.940
I heard the Mongolian Chop Squad made it
to the top 10 in the U.S. College charts.

20:05.940 --> 20:07.240
Uh-huh...

20:07.240 --> 20:10.610
You could say that's quite
a big hit for that kind of music.

20:11.750 --> 20:13.080
I guess the movie worked.

20:13.080 --> 20:16.520
If they weren't from some
minor Indies label from Chicago

20:16.520 --> 20:18.640
they woulda done a lot better, I think.

20:20.750 --> 20:22.920
Maybe you're right.

20:22.920 --> 20:24.190
What do you want?!

20:25.430 --> 20:28.430
Are you here for the dog food, or what?

20:28.430 --> 20:30.860
It's the Grateful Sound...

20:39.540 --> 20:41.170
What the fuck?!

20:51.050 --> 20:52.880
Now, take your time!

20:54.390 --> 20:59.060
Concentrate! You can't be good
at anything unless you concentrate.

20:59.060 --> 21:01.400
Yo! Tanaka-kun...

21:01.400 --> 21:04.190
Oh, Kigata-kun...You're into wrestling?

21:05.400 --> 21:07.740
Well, I have my eye on the Olympics.

21:07.740 --> 21:09.900
That's impressive!

21:09.900 --> 21:14.910
You and Hiromi-san get on well, don't you?

21:14.910 --> 21:16.540
Oh...we do?

21:18.580 --> 21:26.320
Hm...I think she probably...
likes you.

21:29.590 --> 21:31.260
That's not...

21:31.260 --> 21:32.380
Excuse me...

21:33.590 --> 21:36.930
I saw the movie...
Can I have your autograph?

21:36.930 --> 21:38.760
-Ee...Aah...
-Who, me?!

21:40.270 --> 21:41.830
Koyuki-kun!

21:44.270 --> 21:45.430
Hiromi-chan...

21:50.440 --> 21:52.780
I saw it! The movie...

21:52.780 --> 21:55.450
I went to see it yesterday, with a friend.

21:55.450 --> 21:57.280
Really?

21:57.280 --> 21:59.450
I was so impressed!

21:59.450 --> 22:01.820
You were so big on screen.

22:03.120 --> 22:06.430
The kids in the class
are all talking about you.

22:06.430 --> 22:08.130
Oh?

22:08.130 --> 22:12.660
I wanted to tell you that, so I came
running in my leotard-so embarrassing...

22:14.300 --> 22:15.830
T-Thanks...

22:17.640 --> 22:19.440
Bye!

22:28.150 --> 22:32.650
I still have a lot to learn...

22:32.650 --> 22:36.650
but I'll be happy if the movie
does some good for Beck...

22:38.930 --> 22:41.660
Then...summer will come.

22:50.210 --> 22:52.310
Another minute

22:52.310 --> 22:55.010
Feelin' so fine

22:57.320 --> 22:59.550
You turn the freeze

22:59.550 --> 23:02.280
into warm light

23:04.390 --> 23:07.860
Had a premonition

23:07.860 --> 23:10.530
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.530 --> 23:14.040
My world comin' down

23:14.040 --> 23:16.830
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.610 --> 23:24.780
If you really wanna fly

23:24.780 --> 23:27.540
you gotta let go

23:39.800 --> 23:42.130
Simply the most

23:42.130 --> 23:44.170
big sensation

23:44.170 --> 23:46.970
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:46.970 --> 23:49.240
She's really pretty

23:49.240 --> 23:51.240
One-eyed vision

23:51.240 --> 23:54.080
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.080 --> 23:57.580
Little sister showed me

23:57.580 --> 24:00.250
Really took me for a ride

24:00.250 --> 24:01.920
My world comin' down

24:01.920 --> 24:05.250
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.250 --> 24:09.280
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.660 --> 24:17.000
Next week, Page will
shoot beams from his eyes.

24:17.000 --> 24:20.020
-Next week! Watch it!
-Write Music. Are you serious?!
